.ds AD l
.TH "pocket_conf" "1" "" "" "Pocket SDR"
.SH NAME
pocket_conf \- Configure Pocket SDR FE device registers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
pocket_conf [\-s] [\-a] [\-h] [\-p bus[,port]] [\-v] [conf_file]
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Configure or show the MAX2771 register settings of a Pocket SDR FE device.
If \f[CR]conf_file\f[R] is given, the settings in the configuration file are written to the device registers.
The configuration file is a text file containing MAX2771 register field settings in either keyword=value form or hexadecimal form.
Comments after \f[CR]#\f[R] are ignored.
If \f[CR]conf_file\f[R] is omitted, the command prints the current device settings in the same format.
.PP
Keyword=value form:
.IP
.EX
[CHx]
FCEN     = 97  # ...
FBW      =  0  # ...
F3OR5    =  1  # ...
\&...
.EE
.PP
Hexadecimal form:
.IP
.EX
#CH  ADDR       VALUE
  1  0x00  0xA2241C17
  1  0x01  0x20550288
\&...
.EE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[CR]\-s\f[R]
Save the settings to the device EEPROM.
Saved settings are also loaded automatically at device reset.
.TP
\f[CR]\-a\f[R]
Show all register fields (including reserved bits).
.TP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R]
Read or write registers in hexadecimal form.
.TP
\f[CR]\-p bus[,port]\f[R]
USB bus and port number of the target Pocket SDR FE device.
Without this option, the first device found is selected.
.TP
\f[CR]\-v\f[R]
Print version and exit.
.TP
\f[CR]conf_file\f[R]
Path of the configuration file.
Without this argument, the current register field settings of the device are printed.
.SH REFERENCES
[1] Maxim Integrated, MAX2771 Multiband Universal GNSS Receiver, July 2018.
